[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3545110055","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112902#issuecomment-3545110055","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112902","id":3545110055,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TThYn","user":{"login":"SmallKi","id":37371850,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MzcxODUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37371850?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SmallKi","html_url":"https://github.com/SmallKi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SmallKi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SmallKi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SmallKi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SmallKi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SmallKi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SmallKi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SmallKi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SmallKi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SmallKi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-18T05:25:13Z","updated_at":"2025-11-18T05:25:13Z","body":"Currently, this issue can be temporarily worked around by manually deleting the .dll file before rebuilding. However, the core problem is that the build tool incorrectly assumes the existing .dll is up-to-date and skips overwriting it. This is particularly misleading because the build process reports success, giving the false impression that the latest code has been applied.\nTo address this, could we have an option to either:\nForce overwrite the .dll on every build, ensuring the latest code is always used?\nOr, show warning if there has a newer build result after rebuilding, and provide a manual \"Clean\" button within the editor to clear previous build artifacts?","author_association"